SUMMARY:Postcolonial Motion: Taxis and Travelogues
LOCATION:Anthology Film Archives\, 32 Second Avenue\, Manhattan
DESCRIPTION:While not as long-standing as the romance with trains\, cinem
 a has a love affair with taxis. A cab ride is often more than just a mean
 s of getting from one place to another. The taxi is a cinematic apparatus
  in motion\, a confessional\, an urban microcosm\, a transition\, a tempo
 rary intimacy\, an archive of daily life\, a nightmare of forced conversa
 tion\, an eavesdropper’s dream. Yet beneath such metap… https://www.a
 nthologyfilmarchives.org/film_screenings/calendar?view=list&month=11&year
 =2026#showing-62218
URL:https://www.anthologyfilmarchives.org/film_screenings/calendar?view=l
 ist&month=11&year=2026#showing-62218
